> It isn't. The grammar is completely different from that of any other language
> (except, of course, Loglan).

I'd suggest that the grammar of Lojban does bear a significant
resemblance in higher-level form to the grammar of predicate calculus,
if not in the nitty-gritty surface of it, sufficient that it's worth
mentioning alongside Loglan. It's certainly making things easier for
me.

But I suppose that is probably neither surprising nor relevant to many people.

-Jonathan


